
  The plan is saved at [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/plans/2026-10-02-deploys-page.md[39m and isn't committed. As you asked, I haven't
  started implementing.

  [1mThe plan in three tasks:[0m
  1. [1mPage renders the table:[0m a new [38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m with [38;5;153mrenderDeploys(snapshot, query)[39m. It shows the header with
     the snapshot time, the seven columns, newest first, colored status chips, and durations like "4m 12s" (or "running"
     for a deploy in progress).
  2. [1mFilter, sorting, empty state, fallbacks:[0m the environment dropdown keeps the current sort, the Service and Started
     sort links keep the filter, "No deploys in staging" replaces the table when nothing matches, and unknown
     [38;5;153menv[39m/[38;5;153msort[39m/[38;5;153mdir[39m values fall back to the defaults.
  3. [1mRoute and nav:[0m adds [38;5;153m/deploys[39m to [38;5;153mROUTES[39m so it gets the existing 503 "Snapshot unavailable" handling, and a "Deploys"
     nav link after "Services". Server tests cover a missing snapshot and one with broken JSON.

  [1mThe main design choice:[0m the page is built entirely from the template's [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m components ([38;5;153mpageHeader[39m, [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m,
  [38;5;153mselectField[39m, [38;5;153mdataTable[39m, [38;5;153mstatusChip[39m, [38;5;153memptyState[39m). It does not copy [38;5;153msrc/pages/services.js[39m, which builds its own
  escaping, [38;5;153m<select>[39m, [38;5;153m.pill[39m chips and table. The plan tells the implementer this explicitly. As a result there are no
  CSS changes and no edits to [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m.

  [1mCheck:[0m I ran the plan's code and tests in a throwaway copy of the repo. The suite goes from 19 to 24, 34 and then 38
  passing tests after each task, and the "should fail" step of each task really does fail first.

  [1mThree things I decided where the spec wasn't explicit:[0m
  - [1mFallbacks are per parameter.[0m With [38;5;153m?sort=service&dir=sideways[39m, the valid sort is kept and only [38;5;153mdir[39m falls back to its
    default of [38;5;153mdesc[39m, which gives Service Z→A. The other option would be to reset the whole sort when any part of it is
    invalid.
  - [1mEmpty snapshot with no filter.[0m If there are no deploys at all and no environment is selected, the page says "No
    deploys". The spec only words the filtered case.
  - [1mLong durations stay in minutes.[0m A deploy that runs over an hour shows as e.g. "75m 0s", following the spec's
    "minutes and seconds".

  Tell me if you want any of these changed. Once you're happy with the plan, I'll run it with subagent-driven
  development.

